diff --git a/LOCAL-SONY-NOTES.md b/LOCAL-SONY-NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6d5f107
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LOCAL-SONY-NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Local non-root Sony investigation
+
+Based on upstream 9ef40c1de85b757cbf75dbea174a24b99a0e50a3. MIT attribution and font license are retained.
+
+The old build-and-install entry points are deliberately blocked in this branch. Build, installation, preferred HOME writes, and recovery are separate operations in the enclosing investigation project. Do not run tools/disable.*, tools/restore.*, example debloat lists, or PROMPT.md against this TV. They are preserved as upstream review evidence, not approved instructions.
+
+Local changes:
+- Add a separate LEANBACK_LAUNCHER filter, permitting app-list access and explicit testing with stock Home enabled.
+- Remove unrelated vendor-specific hidden apps and the assumed MediaTek Live TV package. Live TV stays omitted until a Sony integration is discovered and tested. The physical Inputs/TV controls remain available.
+- Use AGP 8.13.1, Gradle 8.13 with its official distribution checksum, and installed build-tools 36.0.0. Set minSdk 28 for this confirmed Android 9 TV (the upstream style uses API 28 fontVariationSettings). Keep targetSdk 29, compileSdk 34, application ID, and HOME component unchanged. Add the missing German dream_name string found by lint.
+- Permit a local debug signing key through TVHOME_DEBUG_KEY. No permissions are granted at install time.
+
+The enclosing scripts/Build-Vibehack.ps1 builds only. scripts/Install-Apk.ps1 separately validates the recorded firmware, user, stock HOME availability and APK identity before installing only an absent package. No automatic update, default switch, permission grant, debloat, screensaver change or stock-Home disabling occurs.
+
+Sony Home priority 2 versus an ordinary app's priority 0 may prevent genuine default switching. A successful set-home-activity response alone does not establish success. See the enclosing firmware report and live test records.
